{
  "schema": "alran.store.packages/v1",
  "note": "Plugins that cannot be assembled from Skills alone, because they carry scripts or a hook. scripts/vendor-package.mjs copies them from a local clone into packages/<id>/. Every upstream file is pinned by SHA-256 ('pins'): the scripts and the hook were read line by line, the Skill text was checked by rules (no invisible characters, no data URIs, no instruction-override phrases, every cross-reference lands on a Skill the package carries). The run stops when an upstream file differs, appears or disappears. After reading the change, 'node scripts/vendor-package.mjs --work <dir> --pin' accepts it. The changes made to upstream files are listed in 'patches' and 'omit' and are written to PATCHES.md inside the package.",
  "packages": [
    {
      "id": "superpowers",
      "name": "superpowers",
      "displayName": "Superpowers",
      "description": "A software-development workflow for the agent: brainstorm a design, write a plan, work through it test-first with reviews, and finish the branch. Fourteen Skills, and a session-start hook that introduces them.",
      "author": "Jesse Vincent",
      "category": "Code",
      "license": "MIT",
      "repo": "https://github.com/obra/superpowers",
      "clone": "obra_superpowers",
      "packageJson": "package.json",
      "commit": "22f0b463e7a5e579904dd6211a520321035526f7",
      "copy": [
        {
          "from": "skills",
          "to": "skills"
        },
        {
          "from": "hooks/session-start",
          "to": "hooks/session-start"
        },
        {
          "from": "hooks/run-hook.cmd",
          "to": "hooks/run-hook.cmd"
        }
      ],
      "omit": [
        {
          "path": "skills/diagnosing-superpowers",
          "reason": "It reads the session transcripts of the host tool and prepares them for a public GitHub issue on the Superpowers repository (`gh issue create --repo obra/superpowers`). Its session discovery looks for another harness's files, and what it does goes to a third party. It is a support channel to the upstream project, not part of the workflow."
        }
      ],
      "patches": [
        {
          "file": "skills/brainstorming/scripts/server.cjs",
          "find": "const SUPERPOWERS_TELEMETRY_DISABLED = TELEMETRY_DISABLE_ENV_VARS.some(name => isTruthyEnv(process.env[name]));",
          "replace": "const SUPERPOWERS_TELEMETRY_DISABLED = true; // Alran store: never load the remote brand logo",
          "reason": "The visual-companion page loads a logo from https://primeradiant.com in the user's browser every time it is shown, unless an environment variable says not to. That is a request to a third party that the user never agreed to. With this line the page shows the text brand only, which is what upstream shows when the variable is set. The server itself is unchanged: it listens on 127.0.0.1, needs a per-session key, and makes no outbound request."
        }
      ],
      "hooks": {
        "SessionStart": [
          {
            "matcher": "startup|clear|compact",
            "hooks": [
              {
                "type": "command",
                "command": "bash \"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/session-start\"",
                "commandWindows": "\"${PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/run-hook.cmd\" session-start",
                "timeout": 10
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "hooksReason": "Upstream's hooks/hooks.json uses the handler fields `shell` and `powershell`, which the Alran package format skips, so its hook would never run. This file registers the same two scripts (unchanged) in the Alran format: the session-start script starts with an explicit `bash`, because archives do not keep the executable bit.",
      "exampleQueries": [
        "Brainstorm a design for this feature before we write any code",
        "Write an implementation plan from this spec",
        "This test fails sometimes: debug it systematically"
      ],
